    "hair_back (back hair): config.cloth.\"back hair\" -> 1 tree(s) per side of the eye axis, from head, rooted on the eye line and tipped 4 px above its bottom, a 1-link trunk forking into 2 branches, 3 links root to tip (hairback_r0_, hairback_r0a_, hairback_r0b_, hairback_l0_, hairback_l0a_, hairback_l0b_); 10 constraint(s), physics on every link, wind 1 -> 8 and gravity 4 -> 24 root to tip (multipliers of the consumer's environment; no direction is drafted), no idle key; the recipe's own defaults, measured on its synthetic fixture (AUTHORING §3): length_ratio 0.5, strength 100/100/50",
    "hair_front (head:front hair): bang_r, bang_c, bang_l are a template, not its locks — columns at 0.25, 0.5 and 0.75 of the face box's width, along the head's down axis (the eye line's perpendicular, roll 3.468 degrees), each rooted on the part's art; the opaque shape does not separate the locks painted inside one mass of hair, so a lock that runs elsewhere is not followed — move the chains onto the locks",
    "hair_front (head:front hair): config.cloth.\"front hair\" -> bang_r, bang_c, bang_l carry physics on both links (bang_r and bang_l the edge's strength, bang_c the trunk's; wind and gravity on the recipe's root-to-tip ramp over their two links) and no idle key; the recipe's chains, links and split shape the hanging strands, not the fringe",
    "hairpin (full:headwear): wraps a tail config.cloth.\"back hair\" drafts — 15050 of its 32314 px lie over hair_back's art, nearest hair_back's spans head's fixed segment 943, hairback_r0_0 5721, hairback_r0a_0 819, hairback_r0b_0 398, hairback_l0_0 5630, hairback_l0a_0 419, hairback_l0b_0 1120 px — so its mesh's segments are those spans and it rides the links hairback_r0_0, hairback_r0a_0, hairback_r0b_0, hairback_l0_0, hairback_l0a_0, hairback_l0b_0 with the tail, not head; no headwear bone, pendant or strand chain is drafted for it (issue #391)",
    "limb arm_r: handwear_r (full:handwear-r) is cut at the r_elbow joint into upperarm_r on sleeve_r0 and forearm_r (with the hand) on sleeve_r1, each rigid on its link with weight 1 — a bend is a rotation at the joint; assemble with this limbs block cuts the layer, and the forearm carries a cap past the elbow (its line counts the cap's pixels, and names any the layer does not hold)",
